        "**1. Explain the properties of the F-distribution.**\n",
        "\n",
        "The F-distribution is a continuous probability distribution commonly used in statistical hypothesis testing, particularly in analysis of variance (ANOVA), regression analysis, and comparing variances (F-test).\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Properties of the F-Distribution (Point-Wise)**  \n",
        "1. **Definition**: Ratio of two independent chi-square distributed variables normalized by their degrees of freedom.  \n",
        "2. **Non-Negative**: \\( F \\geq 0 \\), as it is based on variances.  \n",
        "3. **Right-Skewed**: Skewed to the right, becoming more symmetric as degrees of freedom increase.  \n",
        "4. **Degrees of Freedom**: Defined by two parameters: \\( d_1 \\) (numerator) and \\( d_2 \\) (denominator).  \n",
        "5. **Mean**: Exists for \\( d_2 > 2 \\), given by \\( E[F] = \\frac{d_2}{d_2 - 2} \\).  \n",
        "6. **Variance**: Exists for \\( d_2 > 4 \\), given by  \n",
        "   \\[\n",
        "   \\text{Var}(F) = \\frac{2 d_2^2 (d_1 + d_2 - 2)}{d_1 (d_2 - 2)^2 (d_2 - 4)}\n",
        "   \\]  \n",
        "7. **Asymptotic Normality**: Approaches normality as \\( d_1 \\) and \\( d_2 \\) increase.  \n",
        "8. **Used for Hypothesis Testing**: Key in **ANOVA, regression analysis, and variance comparison (F-test)**.  "
      ],
